===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|cu|ru}} {{term|sc=Cyrs|бракъ|tr=brakŭ|lang=cu}}, from {{etyl|sla-pro|ru}} {{term/t|sla-pro|*borkъ}}.

====Noun====
{{ru-noun|tr=brak|g=m|a=i}}

# [[marriage]], [[matrimony]]

=====Declension=====
{{ru-noun-inan-vel-1||бра́к}}

=====Related terms=====
* [[брачный]]
* [[брачующийся]]

===Etymology 2===
Via {{etyl|pl|ru}} {{term|brak|lang=pl}}, from {{etyl|gml|ru}} {{term|brak||flaw, defect; breaking|lang=gml}}. Compare modern German {{term|Brack|lang=de}} and English {{term|break|lang=en}}.

====Noun====
{{ru-noun|tr=brak|g=m|a=i}}

# [[flaw]], [[defect]]
# {{context|uncountable|lang=ru}} [[defective]] [[goods]], [[waste]], [[spoilage]], [[reject]]s

=====Declension=====
{{ru-noun-inan-vel-1||бра́к}}

=====Related terms=====
